    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning` on owner creation, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern. It's `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349 owners** (inclusive) at create time \u2014 approaching the hard limit of 50, which `RequireCityCapacity` still rejects with 409 unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **New pipeline step** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/AssignCapacityWarning.java`: counts existing owners in the city using the *same* `findAll().stream().filter(city)` logic as `RequireCityCapacity`, then sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40 && count < RequireCityCapacity.CAPACITY`. It runs after `BuildOwner` (city set) and before `SaveOwner` (new owner not counted).\n- **Wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignCapacityWarning` between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `assignPossibleDuplicate`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n- **Domain model** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added the `capacity_warning` column field with getter/setter.\n- **Response mapping** \u2014 `mapper/OwnerMapper.java`: added the `capacityWarning` mapping (null-safe, defaults false), so it serializes on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **OpenAPI schema** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property (this is what generates the `OwnerDto` field).\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added `capacity_warning` to all four (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` (`coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures.\n\nI referenced the counting rule from `RequireCityCapacity` deliberately so the warning tracks the same limit it approaches \u2014 including that both count *all* owners in the city (deleted owners included), consistent with the existing hard-limit behavior.",
